# ntdll: Use shared XState config for emulated XState on ARM64.
# https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/12683 state=merged
# !12610 implemented in-process xstate config for ARM64EC, which matches released Windows versions. However, the experimental Windows version fills USD xstate config instead. This is generally better for the compatibility as an application can use USD directly as well.

I was looking at this in the context of AVX on wow64. The released Windows version does not seem to support that at all in ntdll; it allows enabling AVX instructions emulation, but OS support is just not present. In experimental Windows the support is still not complete (in particular, getting and setting AVX context is only partially supported), but xstate-related functions work fine and AVX is enabled by default. With this series, functions for manipulating xstate work fine on Wine as well.
